{"title":"Career roadmap · Field Researcher","role":"Field Researcher","summary":"A Field Researcher collects and analyses primary information from communities, institutions, environments, or geographic regions through interviews, surveys, observation, focus groups, ethnography, mapping, and field documentation.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"A Field Researcher collects and analyses primary information from communities, institutions, environments, or geographic regions through interviews, surveys, observation, focus groups, ethnography, mapping, and field documentation."},{"type":"p","text":"With Tribal Studies / Regional Studies / Area Studies, the strongest pathway is toward research involving indigenous and tribal communities, regional cultures, livelihoods, development, migration, social change, governance, land and resource use, public services, and cultural heritage."},{"type":"p","text":"The student should build a combination of:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Area Knowledge","Field Research","Ethnography","Data","GIS","Ethics","Report Writing"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Field Research Intern, Research Assistant"},{"text":"Data collection and field support"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Field Researcher, Field Investigator"},{"text":"Interviews, surveys, observation"}],[{"text":"Developing"},{"text":"Research Associate, Field Coordinator"},{"text":"Research execution and coordination"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Senior Researcher, Research Analyst"},{"text":"Research design and analysis"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Research Specialist, Project Lead"},{"text":"Leading field studies"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Research Manager, Programme Research Lead"},{"text":"Multi-site research and teams"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Tribal Research Specialist, Social Impact Researcher"},{"text":"Domain expertise"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Tribal, Regional & Social Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tribal studies"},{"text":"Anthropology"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Regional studies"},{"text":"Indian society"},{"text":"Rural sociology"},{"text":"Social geography"},{"text":"Development studies"},{"text":"Political science"},{"text":"Cultural studies"},{"text":"Indigenous studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tribal communities"},{"text":"Indigenous knowledge systems"},{"text":"Social institutions"},{"text":"Kinship"},{"text":"Culture"},{"text":"Livelihoods"},{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Regional identities"},{"text":"Social change"},{"text":"Development challenges"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic reading"},{"text":"Source evaluation"},{"text":"Note-taking"},{"text":"Research writing"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Ethical research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Regional Community Profile"},{"type":"p","text":"Document a selected community/region's:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Demographics"},{"text":"Livelihoods"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Health access"},{"text":"Infrastructure"},{"text":"Cultural practices"},{"text":"Major development challenges"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Research should use informed consent and protect participant privacy."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Field Research Methods"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from theoretical understanding to primary data collection."},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative methods"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Participant observation"},{"text":"Ethnography"},{"text":"Semi-structured interviews"},{"text":"Oral history"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Key-informant interviews"},{"text":"Case studies"},{"text":"Life histories"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative methods"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Questionnaires"},{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Cross-tabulation"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Basic statistical analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Field tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"KoboToolbox"},{"text":"ODK"},{"text":"Google Forms"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"GPS/GNSS basics"},{"text":"Mobile data collection"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"h","text":"Community Needs Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct a supervised study covering:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Question","Sampling","Fieldwork","Data Collection","Analysis","Findings","Recommendations"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Regional Specialisation & Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a geographical or thematic area."},{"type":"h","text":"1. Tribal Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Livelihoods"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Healthcare access"},{"text":"Indigenous knowledge"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Development programmes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Indigenous Culture"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Language"},{"text":"Oral traditions"},{"text":"Art"},{"text":"Music"},{"text":"Festivals"},{"text":"Material culture"},{"text":"Cultural heritage"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Livelihoods"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Agriculture"},{"text":"Forest-based livelihoods"},{"text":"Handicrafts"},{"text":"Informal economy"},{"text":"Employment"},{"text":"Entrepreneurship"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Migration"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Seasonal migration"},{"text":