al writing"},{"text":"Community mobilisation"}]}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Entry level"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Field Research Intern"},{"text":"Research Intern"},{"text":"Field Investigator"},{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Survey Assistant"},{"text":"Community Research Assistant"},{"text":"Documentation Assistant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Field Researcher"},{"text":"Field Research Executive"},{"text":"Social Researcher"},{"text":"Community Researcher"},{"text":"Research Associate"},{"text":"Field Coordinator"},{"text":"Research Coordinator"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tribal Researcher"},{"text":"Ethnographic Researcher"},{"text":"Development Researcher"},{"text":"Social Impact Researcher"},{"text":"Migration Researcher"},{"text":"Regional Research Analyst"},{"text":"GIS Research Analyst"},{"text":"Cultural Researcher"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Researcher"},{"text":"Research Specialist"},{"text":"Research Project Manager"},{"text":"Research Lead"},{"text":"Research Programme Manager"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What Employers May Test"},{"type":"h","text":"Field research"},{"type":"p","text":"How would you approach a community before beginning data collection?"},{"type":"h","text":"Sampling"},{"type":"p","text":"How would you select participants for a study involving a geographically dispersed population?"},{"type":"h","text":"Interviewing"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a semi-structured interview guide for studying livelihood changes."},{"type":"h","text":"Ethics"},{"type":"p","text":"How would you obtain informed consent in a community with varying literacy levels?"},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse survey data and identify the most significant socioeconomic patterns."},{"type":"h","text":"GIS"},{"type":"p","text":"Map access to schools or healthcare facilities and identify underserved areas."},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"How would you identify themes from 50 interview transcripts?"},{"type":"h","text":"Practical assignment"},{"type":"p","text":"The candidate may be given a community-development research problem and asked to prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research question"},{"text":"Sampling strategy"},{"text":"Interview/survey instrument"},{"text":"Fieldwork plan"},{"text":"Ethical safeguards"},{"text":"Data-analysis approach"},{"text":"Expected findings"},{"text":"Policy recommendations"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Strong options"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Anthropology"},{"text":"MA Sociology"},{"text":"MA Tribal Studies"},{"text":"MA Development Studies"},{"text":"MA Rural Development"},{"text":"MA Social Work"},{"text":"MA Regional Studies"},{"text":"MA Area Studies"},{"text":"MA Human Rights"},{"text":"MA Public Policy"},{"text":"MA Geography"},{"text":"MSc GIS/Remote Sensing"},{"text":"Development Economics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research route"},{"type":"p","text":"For specialist research:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA","MA/Master's","Research Assistant","PhD"]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential doctoral areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tribal studies"},{"text":"Anthropology"},{"text":"Sociology"},{"text":"Development studies"},{"text":"Geography"},{"text":"Indigenous studies"},{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Environmental studies"}]}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Potential master's areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indigenous Studies"},{"text":"Anthropology"},{"text":"Development Studies"},{"text":"International Development"},{"text":"Area Studies"},{"text":"Regional Studies"},{"text":"Migration Studies"},{"text":"Social Research"},{"text":"Public Policy"},{"text":"Human Geography"},{"text":"Environmental Justice"},{"text":"Rural Development"},{"text":"GIS/Geospatial Science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong combinations"},{"type":"h","text":"Indigenous Studies + GIS"},{"type":"h","text":"Anthropology + Data Science"},{"type":"h","text":"Development Studies + Impact Evaluation"},{"type":"h","text":"Area Studies + Geopolitics"},{"type":"h","text":"Social Research + Data Analytics"},{"type":"h","text":"Environmental Studies + Indigenous Knowledge"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Field Research Intern","Research Assistant / Field Investigator","Field Researcher","Research Associate","Senior Researcher","Research Specialist","Research Project Manager","Research Programme Lead","Research Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Development route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Field Researcher","Field Coordinator","Programme Research Officer","Monitoring & Evaluation Specialist","Programme Research Manager","Impact / Research Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 Career Evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Field research will increasingly combine human-centred qualitative research with mobile data collection, GIS, remote sensing, AI-assisted analysis, and participatory digital platforms."},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Social Impact Data Analyst"},{"text":"Digital Ethnography Researcher"},{"text":"Community Data Specialist"},{"text":"Indigenous Knowledge Researcher"},{"text":"Geospatial Social Researcher"},{"text":"AI-Assisted Qualitative Researcher"},{"text":"Digital Development Researcher"},{"text":"Climate & Community Researcher"},{"text":"Participatory GIS Specialist"},{"text":"Social Research Data Scientist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Future field-research workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Community Engagement","Mobile Data Collection","GIS / Remote Sensing","Qualitative + Quantitative Data","AI-Assisted Analysis","Human Validation","Community Feedback","Research Findings","Policy / Programme Action"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI can help transcribe, classify, translate, summarise, and analyse large datasets, but community consent, cultural context, privacy, interpretation, and research ethics must remain human-led."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"flow","items":["Tribal/Regional Studies","Anthropology","Sociology","Development Studies"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Field research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Ethnography","Interviews","Focus Groups","Surveys","Participant Observation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","Statistics","Power BI","SQL","R/Python"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Field technology"},{"type":"flow","items":["KoboToolbox","ODK","GPS/GNSS","Mobile Data Collection"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Geospatial"},{"type":"flow","items":["QGIS","Spatial Analysis","Remote Sensing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research Design","Qualitative Coding","Impact Evaluation","Academic Writing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"flow","items":["Community Engagement","Cultural Sensitivity","Ethics","Stakeholder Management"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"flow","items":["Digital Ethnography","AI-Assisted Research","Social Data Science","Participatory GIS"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"h","text":"0–2 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Field Research Intern","Research Assistant","Field Researcher"]},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Field Researcher","Research Associate","Field Coordinator"]},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Senior Researcher","Research Specialist","Research Project Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"8+ years"},{"type":"p","text":"Research Programme Lead → Research Director / Senior Research Consultant"},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"For BA Tribal Studies / Regional Studies / Area Studies → Field Researcher, build:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Area Knowledge","Ethnographic Research","Quantitative Methods","GIS","Mobile Data Collection","M&E","Research Ethics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest candidates are not simply good at conducting surveys. They can enter communities ethically, build trust, collect reliable primary data, combine qualitative and quantitative evidence, map spatial patterns, understand local cultural context, and translate findings into useful research or policy recommendations."},{"type":"p","text":"A postgraduate degree in Anthropology, Tribal Studies, Development Studies, Sociology, Geography, Public Policy, or a related field is particularly valuable for progressing from fieldwork into specialist research and research-leadership roles."},{"type":"p","text":"1548 | BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours) | Tribal Studies / Regional Studies / Area Studies | Field Researcher"}]}]}